---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import VesselTable from '../components/VesselTable.astro';
import data from '../data/pipeline.json';

const { vessels, summary } = data;
const n = (v: number, d = 0) =>
  v.toLocaleString('en-GB', { minimumFractionDigits: d, maximumFractionDigits: d });

const ranked = vessels
  .filter((v) => v.departureLapses > 0)
  .sort((a, b) => b.departureLapses - a.departureLapses);

const fastest = [...ranked].sort(
  (a, b) => b.fastestKnWhileClaimingStationary - a.fastestKnWhileClaimingStationary)[0];
---
<Base title="Forgot on departure — who kept saying 'moored' while moving">
  <h1>Forgot on departure</h1>

  <p class="lede prose">
    The ship left. The dial stayed on <code>Moored</code> or <code>At anchor</code>.
  </p>

  <ul class="stats">
    <li class="stat alarm"><b>{n(summary.departureLapses)}</b><span>position reports</span></li>
    <li class="stat"><b>{ranked.length}</b><span>vessels</span></li>
    <li class="stat alarm"><b>{n(fastest?.fastestKnWhileClaimingStationary ?? 0, 1)}</b><span>fastest, in knots, while "moored"</span></li>
  </ul>

  <p class="prose">
    A moored ship is never perfectly still — tide, wind and GPS noise all register. So the threshold
    isn't a guess: across every fix claiming a stationary status, speed decays smoothly to a minimum
    at <strong>2–3 knots</strong> and then rises again. Two populations, and the trough between them
    is where one ends and the other begins. Everything listed here is above it.
  </p>

  <p class="prose note">
    Ranked by count here rather than share, because the denominator is every position report a
    vessel sent — tens of thousands — so the percentages are all small and rank almost nothing.
    {fastest && (
      <> The stand-out is <a href={`/vessel/${fastest.mmsi}`}>{fastest.name ?? fastest.mmsi}</a> at
      {' '}{n(fastest.fastestKnWhileClaimingStationary, 1)} knots, which is service speed.</>
    )}
  </p>

  <VesselTable vessels={ranked} kind="departure" />
</Base>
